# LOOP C — INDEPENDENT AUDIT, TAT-QA WP-1 (final artifacts)

**Nature of document:** advisory audit report. I report; I do not repair. Adjudication belongs to the owner.
**Audited object & baseline:** WP-1 thin runner final artifacts vs. `WP0_TATQA_ADAPTER_CHECKER_CONTRACT_v1.md` incl. revision 1.1. Baseline (known, *not* new findings): run-1 `SOFTWARE_NOT_QUALIFIED: hidden_gold_search` fail-closed, already diagnosed in spec §4 as an over-broad check definition. A re-report of that is a known case.
**Independence declaration:** I did not build any audited artifact (Loop A did). Per anti-anchoring clause 1 I read the **binding spec and acceptance package first**, then the **code**, and only then the author receipts — so the code-level conclusions below were formed before I saw any PASS claim. I did not read `loop_a_prompt*.md` conclusions before forming them. Mitigation: every number below is recomputed from a primary carrier (`sha256sum`, `grep`, `jq`, hand arithmetic) or read at a cited line. Where I re-ran an author check I say so.

**Method note:** `python3 -c` is denied by my permission gate, so the count/JSON checks are **statically replicated** with `grep`/`jq`/`sha256sum` (as the brief anticipates). I did **not** run `run_fixtures.py` — `write_outputs` mutates receipts, which would violate read-only. Loop D runs the suite natively.

